# Draft knowledge entry: Boost CMake versioned shared-library links on HarmonyOS PC
id: DRAFT-boost-cmake-hmdfs-versioned-soname-links
trigger_tool: cmake|conan|install
phase: package|install|runtime
error_signature: "BoostInstall.cmake|BOOST_INSTALL_NO_VERSIONED_LIBS|libboost_.*\\.so\\.[0-9]|HMDFS|versioned shared-library symlink|Function not implemented"

severity: 2
category: boost|cmake|install|shared-library|ohos
match_keywords: BoostInstall.cmake, BOOST_INSTALL_NO_VERSIONED_LIBS, versioned libs, libboost_python312.so, shared library symlink, HMDFS, OHOS

title: Boost CMake recipes on OHOS should suppress versioned shared-library install links without dropping SONAME
root_cause: >
  Boost's CMake install helper can create versioned shared-library outputs or symlink-style
  install entries for shared libraries. On OHOS/HMDFS package staging this can fail or produce
  package metadata that does not match the unversioned libraries consumed by Conan CMakeDeps.
affected_scope: >
  Boost CMake-based shared-library Conan recipes on HarmonyOS PC, especially recipes that add
  compiled components such as filesystem, program_options, system, or Boost.Python.
verification_cmd: |
  rg -n "BOOST_INSTALL_NO_VERSIONED_LIBS|BoostInstall.cmake|VERSIONED" archives/b/boost/1.90.0.2.1
  conan create archives/b/boost/1.90.0.2.1 -pr:h ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -r=ohpcd --build=missing

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: gate-boost-versioned-install-links
rec_description: >
  On OHOS, set BOOST_INSTALL_NO_VERSIONED_LIBS and patch BoostInstall.cmake so versioned
  shared-library install outputs are skipped when the variable is enabled. Do not drop linker
  SONAME metadata while doing this; add an explicit unversioned DT_SONAME for each shared Boost
  target and verify that unversioned libboost_*.so files and Conan component targets are still
  installed and consumed.
rec_command: |
  tc.variables["BOOST_INSTALL_NO_VERSIONED_LIBS"] = True
  # Patch BoostInstall.cmake:
  # if(TYPE STREQUAL "SHARED_LIBRARY" AND BOOST_INSTALL_NO_VERSIONED_LIBS)
  #   target_link_options(${LIB} PRIVATE "-Wl,-soname,$<TARGET_FILE_NAME:${LIB}>")
  # endif()
  # if((TYPE STREQUAL "SHARED_LIBRARY" OR TYPE STREQUAL "EXECUTABLE") AND NOT BOOST_INSTALL_NO_VERSIONED_LIBS)
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: boost-cmake-install-patch

fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: inspect-installed-package-layout
fallback_description: >
  If install or consumer linking still fails, inspect the package lib directory and generated CMake
  targets before changing SONAME or copying files. Keep the public component names stable and avoid
  shipping broken symlink entries.
fallback_command: |
  find package -name "libboost*.so*" -o -name "*Boost*Targets*.cmake"
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: package-layout-diagnosis

forbid_1_pattern: "post-package symlink farm|copy versioned libs blindly|remove SONAME validation"
forbid_1_reason: Blind file duplication can desynchronize library filenames, SONAMEs, and generated CMake targets.
forbid_1_consequence: Downstream consumers may link one name while the runtime loader resolves another.
forbid_2_pattern: "disable shared libraries to avoid BoostInstall.cmake"
forbid_2_reason: Consumers such as Boost.Python and eigenpy require the shared-library path to be validated.
forbid_2_consequence: The dependency may no longer satisfy the downstream package's real runtime requirements.

principles: install-layout-validation, conan-component-consumer-test, ohos-filesystem-aware-packaging
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of: eigenpy-3.13.0

